WEBVTT

NOTE Captions of the mcp-audit explainer, from its narration (#106).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
Audits rarely fail for lack of automation.

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:07.842
They suffer when auditors drown in
documents, spreadsheets and follow-ups,

3
00:00:07.842 --> 00:00:10.080
and run out of time for judgement.

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:16.038
The MCP audit platform is built on one
idea: AI does the groundwork, and the

5
00:00:16.038 --> 00:00:17.920
auditor makes the calls.

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.190
Everything AI writes arrives as a
proposal.

7
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:25.430
Every change is versioned, with who made
it and on whose behalf.

8
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.498
And missing evidence means no reasonable
assurance, never an invented

9
00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:31.600
non-conformity.

10
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.170
Here is how an audit runs, in five steps.

11
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.070
One: set up.

12
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:43.358
Choose the requirements from the library,
such as NIS 2 or ISO 27001, define the

13
00:00:43.358 --> 00:00:47.210
scopes, and record the auditee's roles and
risks.

14
00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.448
AI can read the risk register and check
the scope against the Statement of

15
00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:52.250
Applicability.

16
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.350
You decide what stays in.

17
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.000
Two: understand the auditee's own rules.

18
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.233
AI reads the policies and procedures and
proposes internal requirements, each with

19
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:06.360
an exact quote and the requirement it
implements.

20
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.190
When a policy changes, every rule is
rechecked against the new version.

21
00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.170
Three: plan.

22
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.940
Enter the fieldwork days, working hours
and exceptions.

23
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:21.488
AI drafts a timetable with an opening
meeting, daily summaries and time for

24
00:01:21.488 --> 00:01:24.580
notes, and the evidence to collect at each
meeting.

25
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:29.820
Documents you already have are linked, so
the plan asks only for what is missing.

26
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.250
Four: run the audit.

27
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.422
On your phone, take notes during each
interview, record promises and suspected

28
00:01:37.422 --> 00:01:39.610
issues, and add photos and files.

29
00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:44.054
Afterwards, AI links the material to the
planned evidence, and the platform

30
00:01:44.054 --> 00:01:47.490
produces the follow-up report for the
people who attended.

31
00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.640
Five: conclude.

32
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:54.480
For every requirement and scope, AI
proposes a finding with a rationale that

33
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.690
cites the evidence.

34
00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:00.900
Only you approve it, and the findings
report holds approved findings only.

35
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.490
It works with what you already use.

36
00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.220
Meeting transcripts from your online
meetings and recording tools.

37
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:10.000
Documents the auditee has already sent.

38
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.270
What you learned in last year's audit.

39
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:18.213
And your own AI assistant: through the MCP
connector, Claude works in the platform

40
00:02:18.213 --> 00:02:20.460
directly, under the same rules.

41
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.340
You also choose where the AI runs.

42
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:28.329
Use a cloud model such as Claude, or keep
everything on your own infrastructure with

43
00:02:28.329 --> 00:02:29.160
a local model.

44
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:34.168
The platform is a single container, and
each engagement can be limited to one

45
00:02:34.168 --> 00:02:36.770
model, or have AI switched off entirely.

46
00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:41.736
The result: more time for interviews and
professional judgement, consistent

47
00:02:41.736 --> 00:02:45.510
coverage, and a full audit trail behind
every conclusion.

48
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.900
Not an automated auditor.

49
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.350
A better-equipped one.
